 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nTechnical Data\n\nEntity Type                                                                Service Operation\n\nRelease State                                                             released\n\nTechnical Name                                                      ContractAccountERPSplitltemGroupByBusinessPartnerlDQueryResponse_In\nNamespace                                                               http://sap.com/xi/FICA/Global rie\nApplication Component                                                FI-CA\n\nWeb Service Definition (Back End)                                 ECC_CONTACC_SP_ITEM_GRP_BYBPQR\nDirection                                                                        inbound\n\nMode                                                                             synchronous\n\nIdempotency                                                                   no\n\nChange/Update Behavior                                               not applicable\n\nP2P Communication Enabled                                         true\n\nBusiness Context and Use\n\nThe inbound operation Find Contract Account Split Item Group by Business Partner ID returns the items of one or more\ncontract accounts of a business partner according to specified selection criteria. The items are grouped with reference to the\noriginal invoice.\n\nSee the Features section for a description of the available selection criteria and the returned fields.\n\nRelated Operations\n\nThe inbound operations Find Contract Account Receivables Payables Register Item by ID and Find Contract Account Split Item\nGroup by Elements return the items of a contract account based on other selection criteria.\n\nYou can use the operation Create Payment Directive to assign Splititems to a PaymentDirective and thus release them for\ncollection by the corresponding payment run. The released SplitItems are grouped together if they are set to be paid by the same\n\npayment method.\n\nFeatures\n\nThis operation returns the Items and Splitltems of a contract account for a specified business partner. Each Item, comprising one\nor more Splitltems, may be open or cleared, or may contain a combination of open and cleared (subordinate) Splititems.\n\nThe corresponding data elements in SAP S/4HANA are:\n\ne Items: OPBEL + OPUPW + OPUPK\n\ne Splitltems: OPUPZ\n\nNote that in the FI-CA back end a cleared split item always points to its clearing document, whereas in this message structure the\n",
